<!-- Font Awesome "user" (free, solid), in its native 448x512 box. The same glyph
     the app's own World Clock rows draw for a followed person, so the list and
     the widget show one mark rather than two that nearly agree.

     iOS uses person.fill instead, which is the one place the two platforms'
     marks are not the same path: SF Symbols has had a head-and-shoulders since
     long before this project's deployment target, so there was nothing to work
     around there. The ship and the anchor went to Font Awesome because SF
     Symbols genuinely lacked them at iOS 15. -->
